{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith","id":1092416,"title":"Are the Unseelie still Sith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-14T12:11:52-07:00","id":1092416,"title":"Are the Unseelie still Sith?","content":"In Star Wars the Sith are often described as a cancer on the Force. The Force was supposed to work in symbiotic harmony, particularly with its users, while the Sith warped and twisted it, and were warped and twisted in return, with their selfishness and hate and adopted a parasitic role with the Force.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie were always cast in a similar role. They were OF the Dreaming but they were also destroyers of the Dreaming, burning out the few fonts of Glamour alive in the world wherever they went. Whether it was through Ravaging or Rhapsody, the Dreaming died in their passing and their was even an entire Unseelie House that was dedicated to the act of perpetual Rhapsody. The other Unseelie Houses were only a marginal step up. Hell, House Eluind who was supposedly Seelie with Unseelie leanings were only a lesser evil. So do the Unseelie exist as parasites that warp and destroy The Dreaming in their unrelenting selfishness? Should the lot of them still be shot on sight for being mustache twirling villains? Has anything changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:25:32-07:00","id":1092418,"title":"","content":"I don't think unseelie ever was evil, and it still isn't. Nor is there anything inherently banality inspiring. <br /> <br /> Unseelie is about freedom and passion, seelie is about order and beauty. Either way could be good or evil, banal or glamorous. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't see how you can blaim Winter or the Shattering or anything like that more on one group more than the other either. <br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately what you've described is a great position for a seelie apologist to take in game, but it's not the kind of thing an ST (or writer for Changeling) should be enforcing on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:27:55-07:00","id":1092420,"title":"","content":"The philosophical discussion comes to an end when the Dreaming has a dying source that the Unseelie actively destroy for a quick fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:33:43-07:00","id":1092426,"title":"","content":"Way more dreamers exists than ever are mused or ravaged by Changelings. Also, it's not like Winter is caused by ravaging, or even rhapsody. If you really want to try to pin it on something the fae have done the biggest culprit is the Right of Ignorance, and even then it probably wouldn't have changed things either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:34:29-07:00","id":1092427,"title":"","content":"Plus, are you talking about banality and glamour, or good and evil? They're not at all the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:24:33-07:00","id":1092457,"title":"","content":"No, I'm talking about how Dreamers are the lifeblood of the dying Dreaming. Every Dreamer destroyed brings Changelings that much closer to Endless Winter. <br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not just talking about artists either. We all know those special people in our lives who have a degree of color, light, or life inside them that others don't and are a ray of light in a gray world. How many of those Dreamers does an Unseelie break in a month?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-14-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:27:42-07:00","id":1092458,"title":"","content":"Ravaging doesn't necessarily destroy the dreamer though. Sure its not ideal, but the world is full of grey areas. can unseelie be evil? sure. but so can seelie. Duke Dray is a perfect example, perhaps Morwyn too (depending on how you look at it). Think of it less as black and white. The unseelie tenants are simple a different outlook , its not better or worse, just... different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:35:49-07:00","id":1092463,"title":"","content":"Again, the combined might of all ravagings and rhapsody throughout history (and lets not forget those aren't purely unseelie activities) are a drop in the bucket towards the total supply of dreamers. Would I, personally, do something like that? No, but I also wouldn't non-consensually enchant someone. But it's not the reason for Winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:41:38-07:00","id":1092468,"title":"","content":"Wellll, with that said.. while on a macro scale, sure, the world is full of people and rolls onwards, but on a micro scale, ravaging/rhapsody is something of a screw over to local fae as far as ultimately decreasing the locally available dreamers/making it harder to find them/rousing the attention of what hunts the supernatural.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Unseelie themselves are noted to overall regard Rhapsody as a severe taboo crime. You can't really call a group the Sith when they'll kill you for eating a dude's soul for power just like the other group would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:51:51-07:00","id":1092472,"title":"","content":"Unseelie houses are not Unseelie, just like the Seelie house are not the Seelie.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:51:57-07:00","id":1092473,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by &quot;local&quot;. Ravaging some Dreamer &quot;owned&quot; by another fae is obviously a dick move at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:57:31-07:00","id":1092476,"title":"","content":"If you're fae not in a particularly sizable city, Dreamers getting more banality-ized (banalized? That sounds wrong) or outright soul dying is way more of a deal, for instance. Even in a larger city, if there's a particularly prevalent swath of banality rising, damage to the local Dreamer communities is going to be noticeable. There were occasional plots to that tune in various bits of material.<br /> <br /> It's part of why I'm not super great with ravaging as a banality causing risk for the fae that do it. Ravaging, it causes problems on various levels, so there should be something legitimately tempting about doing it anyway beyond &quot;quick glamour&quot;, at least just in my own view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:04:23-07:00","id":1092482,"title":"","content":"Do keep in mind that failing should be a banality trigger, not an automatic point (I already brought it up in the errata thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:07:52-07:00","id":1092484,"title":"","content":"Eh, even as a risk of increasing your own banality that makes it feel like something fae would be less inclined to do, yet ravaging is instead a big ol thing such that you get gangs of fae that get up to that sort of activity, and it otherwise is a thing that regularly happens, and people talk about it feeling good and etc.<br /> <br /> Synergy! We're talking about setting vs mechanics in that other thread as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:11:07-07:00","id":1092487,"title":"","content":"I think it's fine. Remember, when you gain glamour you can get rid of temporary banality. And being more inclined to take risks for a quick payout is totally in line with the Unseelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:14:46-07:00","id":1092490,"title":"","content":"Right, but when you're spending glamour to get rid of temporary banality you're further limiting how much you're really getting out of the practice, it takes it further from &quot;a risk&quot;, to &quot;kind of a poor choice&quot;. I suppose I just wish there was more <i>there</i> there to Ravaging, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:29:03-07:00","id":1092499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092458#post1092458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravaging doesn't necessarily destroy the dreamer though. Sure its not ideal, but the world is full of grey areas. can unseelie be evil? sure. but so can seelie. Duke Dray is a perfect example, perhaps Morwyn too (depending on how you look at it). Think of it less as black and white. The unseelie tenants are simple a different outlook , its not better or worse, just... different</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't saying much. Everyone knows that Seelie can be evil, but we pretty much ONLY see the Unseelie as monsters. Hurting people seems to be in their job description. So does not caring about WHO you hurt. All you really see in the examples of Unseelie in the Book of Houses books, which is one of the few places where the Unseelie give IC viewpoints of themselves and the world, is a mixture of greed, selfishness, and cruelty with a ton of pretentiousness thrown in for good measure. Hilariously, the closest I ever came to empathizing with a group of Unseelie was with Kithbook Redcaps because they at least tried to explain WHY they were monsters/Unseelie. I'm just curious if ANYTHING has changed and we see the potential good in the Unseelie now, or if they are still just an evil in the WoD without any real attempt to protagonize them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-14-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:32:35-07:00","id":1092503,"title":"","content":"Again i think its a matter of perception. Ive always viewed unseelie as self serving rather than evil and i think that tone carries into this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:36:22-07:00","id":1092507,"title":"","content":"The unseelie are the only people in current fae organizing a protest movement against the whole glamour starving thing, so there's that (granted the ones doing it are the dupes of the Thallain so.. there's that).<br /> <br /> House Danaan is technically unseelie, though I suppose that they don't super acknowledge that is also admittedly a thing.<br /> <br /> I would say though, in previous editions, some of it was stuff I wasn't fond of, but you certainly had things like Kithbook Redcap's entire big thing of &quot;we are the monsters that fight the other monsters to keep them from killing fae society&quot;, you had the Knights of the Cold Watch, an all unseelie group dedicated to fighting supernatural evil, you had various unseelie npcs here and there who were decent sorts mostly, you had some of the Unseelie Lost Houses being mixed bags of good and bad, so forth.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:56:48-07:00","id":1092518,"title":"","content":"Example primarily Unseelie Kiths include Eshu, Nockers, Redcaps, Satyrs, Clurichauns, and Sluagh. The Houses give a kind of distorted view of things I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:11:19-07:00","id":1092528,"title":"","content":"I don't recall the Eshu, Nockers or Satyrs being primarily unseelie, at least not to the degree Redcaps were for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Houses give a kind of distorted view of things I think. </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Ailil were fine for what they were, and the Unseelie in Lost Houses were generally mixed bags of sorts. The Aesin especially were &quot;we're here to kill the Fomorians and chew bubblegum, and having recently arrived from Arcadia, we don't even understand what bubblegum is&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:33:13-07:00","id":1092543,"title":"","content":"Not to the same degree, but to pull a number out of no where at least 60%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:51:32-07:00","id":1092555,"title":"","content":"Nockers maybe, but that doesn't quite feel exactly right for Eshu or Satyrs.<br /> <br /> edit: I suppose some of that might be npc representation? There have been a fair stretch of seelie satyr and eshu npcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T17:51:14-07:00","id":1092591,"title":"","content":"Saying that Ravaging is Killing the Dreaming is like taking a renown hit in werewolf for riding in a car because &quot;its killing Gaia&quot;. It doesn't help but it sure isn't Reaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:10:38-07:00","id":1092594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092426#post1092426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way more dreamers exists than ever are mused or ravaged by Changelings. Also, it's not like Winter is caused by ravaging, or even rhapsody. If you really want to try to pin it on something the fae have done the biggest culprit is the Right of Ignorance, and even then it probably wouldn't have changed things either way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> on house Leahaun...<br /> <br /> I HATE that they no longer need to commit Rhapsody to reverse aging... im ok with them being able to stall things indefinitely in a freehold but... this really weakens things, a leahaun who commits rhapsody now is doing so to be a sick bastard, not as a grim and dire neccessity now. with him weeping for his victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:28:20-07:00","id":1092601,"title":"","content":"If it make you feel any better, by dialing them back to per week instead of per month for the glamour requirement and by how much comparative glamour they need from musing to reverse aging, it's probably more survivable for them to rely on ravaging. It's not quite the same tragic air I grant you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:40:53-07:00","id":1092607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092594#post1092594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> on house Leahaun...<br /> <br /> I HATE that they no longer need to commit Rhapsody to reverse aging... im ok with them being able to stall things indefinitely in a freehold but... this really weakens things, a leahaun who commits rhapsody now is doing so to be a sick bastard, not as a grim and dire neccessity now. with him weeping for his victim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I found the old version was completely unplayably monsterous. Like &quot;my Seelie legacy is active.. guess i need to go throw myself into traffic&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:52:57-07:00","id":1092616,"title":"","content":"I have a very different approach to playing Changeling I think. If my character has a low Banality I generally look at my legacies, my court, and any oaths I may have sworn, and just stick to that for my character's morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T19:46:11-07:00","id":1092636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092607#post1092607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I found the old version was completely unplayably monsterous. Like &quot;my Seelie legacy is active.. guess i need to go throw myself into traffic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> sighs, intellectualy, the points conceded.<br /> <br /> but I LOVED the tragic romance, thats been killed by this rules rewrite...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T21:00:38-07:00","id":1092648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092636#post1092636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> sighs, intellectualy, the points conceded.<br /> <br /> but I LOVED the tragic romance, thats been killed by this rules rewrite...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I never got a tragic romance off them, just complete and utter bastardry. Now that they don't have to Rhapsody all the time I can see the temptation of a character who's sees themselves as fairly nonbastardish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T06:50:09-07:00","id":1092783,"title":"","content":"another unseelie question?<br /> <br /> it says house Balor has the &quot;Fewest Seelie of any house&quot; Implying its no longer none that their no longer categoricaly incapable of assuming their seelie legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T06:52:22-07:00","id":1092785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092783#post1092783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another unseelie question?<br /> <br /> it says house Balor has the &quot;Fewest Seelie of any house&quot; Implying its no longer none that their no longer categoricaly incapable of assuming their seelie legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct. <br /> <br /> Basically, you can't assume anything in a previous book still applies with C20 (although of course many things can still be brought into your game if you want).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T07:26:44-07:00","id":1092796,"title":"","content":"So one of the goals when I was writing the Courts in C20 was to make sure the Seelie aren't universally squeaky clean good guys and the Unseelie aren't 100% unrepentant villains.<br /> <br /> The approach I tried to take was that they're each two halves of a whole, and that neither they nor the Dreaming could survive without both despite being opposites. Like day and night, nothing can grow without sunlight, but if the night were somehow eliminated, the world quickly become a scorched and barren wasteland. Evening are necessary to erase the heat of the day and for rejuvination, but if the sun never rises again, the world becomes a dead, frozen tundra. Likewise, order ensures you have what you need to survive, but chaos is required to remove things that don't work anymore and introduce something new.<br /> <br /> The Seelie wish to preserve Glamour at all costs, while the Unseelie want to eradicate Banality. The Seelie believe that strength comes from unity, but the Unseelie prize the individual. Neither one is wrong, but their ideals guarantee they'll come into conflict with each other. At the same time though, one without the other is a recipe for disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:57:32-07:00","id":1092833,"title":"","content":"take it &quot;House Balor's Mad Plans<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AppleSDGothicNeo-Regular\">\u2122</span></span>of Total Domination of the world!&quot; Are also no longer canon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:27:48-07:00","id":1092909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092833#post1092833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">take it &quot;House Balor's Mad Plans<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:AppleSDGothicNeo-Regular\">\u2122</span></span>of Total Domination of the world!&quot; Are also no longer canon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well they moved onto a different mad scheme of World domination<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>c20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than scheme<br /> about ways to re-enter Arcadia, however, the Blooded have<br /> a different plan. They intend to conquer the Autumn World<br /> and thereby cut off its supply of Glamour to Arcadia. House<br /> Balor will not grovel and beg to be taken back; the Blooded<br /> will force Arcadia to its knees.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Since we are talking about House Balor I'm not sure their Boon makes as much sense now that the Formorians are no longer immune to banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:05:28-07:00","id":1092968,"title":"","content":"The problem with this all is that certain game mechanics still enforce the idea that Seelie is good and Unseelie is evil:<br /> <br /> Legacies are very strictly defined so that largely 'positive' options are Seelie and largely 'negative' ones are Unseelie. I can see an Unseelie Paladin Legacy who must win at all costs, though, or the Seelie Ringleader for whom order it all.<br /> <br /> Musing and Ravaging Thresholds have the same issue: Musing Thresholds are almost all positive, Ravaging options almost all negative. Why can't an Unseelie muse somebody with anger or jealousy? Sure, they're dark emotions, but they're passion, and could be stirred up and cultivated. And many positive emotions can take dark turns if pushed just right, like the poor Artist driven to madness and self-neglect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:26:22-07:00","id":1092981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092416-are-the-unseelie-still-sith?p=1092968#post1092968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this all is that certain game mechanics still enforce the idea that Seelie is good and Unseelie is evil:<br /> <br /> Legacies are very strictly defined so that largely 'positive' options are Seelie and largely 'negative' ones are Unseelie. I can see an Unseelie Paladin Legacy who must win at all costs, though, or the Seelie Ringleader for whom order it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the legacies more closely there's alot of Seelie ones that basically &quot;Oh there's a lynch mob.. guess I shoudl get a torch&quot;. Unseelie are definately &quot;Fuck you I'll do what i want&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Musing and Ravaging Thresholds have the same issue: Musing Thresholds are almost all positive, Ravaging options almost all negative. Why can't an Unseelie muse somebody with anger or jealousy? Sure, they're dark emotions, but they're passion, and could be stirred up and cultivated. And many positive emotions can take dark turns if pushed just right, like the poor Artist driven to madness and self-neglect. </div> </div> </div>Have to agree that Create anger sticks out in the Ravaging Threshold. Ravaging should make you feel numb and broken, almost &quot;Inspire Depression&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:32:46-07:00","id":1092987,"title":"","content":"I didn't want to stray too far from what the Legacies originally were. I did soften the Unseelie Legacies a bit from 2E so they're not as unambiguously evil. I also introduced a rule that lets you use your secondary Legacy to ignore the Ban from your primary one. The idea is to reinforce the notion that a changeling isn't complete without both her Seelie and Unseelie halves.<br /> <br /> I made a couple of posts in another thread talking about it more starting here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090416#post1090416\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...16#post1090416</a><br /> <br /> Edit to add: I can't give any insight to the musing and ravaging thresholds since I didn't write those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}